From cb2a63755dbb22c2573bbcc45c51e6681caffeb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:25:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Arp: ratchet notes Ball, a ping-pong ball between plates that
 close in and part again

A roll over each half of the ratchet. The first half speeds up into its middle (each gap the one before times r, r
from the ratchet bounce as for the roll), where the ball buzzes at 15 ms. The second half is a roll backwards with
its own, faster ratio (1 - r_p = 1.5 (1 - r)): after the buzz the gaps grow faster than they shrank, so the ball
ends slower than it started, as the arp figure in Pettra "You Are The Seeds" does. With negative bounce the plates
meet at both ends of the ratchet (on the step) and are furthest apart in its middle. Menu Arpeggiator > Ratchet
notes: Auto, 2 ... 8, Roll, Ball; saved as ratchetNotes="254" (older firmware reads it as 8 notes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
